  {%- comment -%}
    THE FINAL TYPOGRAPHY SYSTEM — Aloha, 24 September 2026.

      01 PORTER MEDIUM            navigation / global UI (header + footer);
                                  hover and selected state Porter Light
      02 PORTER LIGHT             section labels / index headings
      03 NOTO SANS MONO MEDIUM    links, CTAs, buttons, references, data,
                                  and ALL numbers
      04 JUNICODE LIGHT           editorial body and information
      05 JUNICODE LIGHT           editorial headlines / display titles
      06 JUNICODE SEMIBOLD ITALIC editorial emphasis / pull lines

    "Once this is implemented, I'd like us to avoid introducing additional
     font weights unless there is a specific reason."

    Two faces below make the Noto rows mechanical rather than a matter of
    remembering:

    HA Mono — Noto Sans Mono Medium declared across the whole weight range.
    Whatever weight a rule asks the record voice for (Luxe asks for 400, the
    Journal build asked for 600 and 700), the browser has exactly one face
    to give it, so the record voice cannot drift off Medium and is never
    synthesised.

    HA Figures — the same file restricted to the digits (and, for Porter, the
    solidus). "If a number appears within text set in Porter or Junicode, the
    number itself should still switch to Noto Sans Mono […] Please don't
    allow the surrounding font to automatically determine the number font."
    It sits at the front of the Junicode and Porter stacks, so a 1970 in a
    Junicode paragraph or the 01 / in a Porter label is drawn in Noto Mono
    Medium without anyone marking it up. `size-adjust` matches its cap
    height to the voice around it (Junicode caps 0.663em, Porter 0.700em,
    Noto 0.714em), so a figure does not stand taller than its capitals.
    Declared italic as well, so a figure inside a pull line stays upright
    Noto rather than a slanted synthesis of it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Mono";
    src: url({{ 'ha-typewriter-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 599;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
