  {%- comment -%}
    THE TYPOGRAPHY OF 2 OCTOBER 2026 — Aloha and Angela, "Website font rules",
    with the About The Circle artboard as the reference for scale. It replaces
    the 24 September roles across the whole site:

      1 TROJA PRO          large page titles (and, as her artboard draws it,
                           every display heading: section and card titles)
      2 PORTER             navigation, menu, small labels, section tags,
                           structural headings; buttons, as drawn
      3 TYPEWRITER         information: body, descriptions, product copy,
                           stories, material notes, prices and data,
                           at 82% opacity in running paragraphs
      4 TYPEWRITER BOLD    standalone numbering only (01, 02, 03)
      5 JUNICODE ITALIC    small personal notes, asides, invitations, emphasis

    Files, from her drive folder (Latin subsets, scripts not kept — rebuild
    with pyftsubset from the originals in docs/typography-2026-10-02/):
      ha-troja.woff2                 GC Troja Pro Regular (Glyphonic)
      ha-typewriter.woff2            typrighter Bold (Jadugar Design Studio)
      ha-junicode-semibold-italic    Junicode SemiBold Italic (SIL OFL)

    ⚠️ LICENCE. Troja and typrighter are commercial desktop fonts. Neither
    file carries a web licence, and a webfont is downloadable by design.
    They are served here, on the unpublished theme, because the client
    sent them for this purpose. A web licence is needed before launch.
    Same position as Porter (risk R1).

    typrighter first came in ONE weight, Bold, so text and numbers shared
    it. Since the Regular arrived (later on 2 October) text is Regular and
    numbers Bold; see HA Text below. Paragraphs stay at 82% opacity. The
    faces between them cover the whole weight range so that no rule, Luxe's
    included, can make the browser synthesise a heavier or lighter version.

    HA Text is the information voice. Its italic slot is Junicode SemiBold
    Italic — typrighter has no italic, and her italic is always Junicode —
    so an <em>, or any italic line in the body voice, becomes role 5 without
    markup. typrighter has no en or em dash, ellipsis or à/è/ñ; those
    characters fall through to Junicode, next in the stack.

    NO NOTO, 4 OCTOBER 2026 (Ivan): "make sure no Noto Sans Mono is placed
    in the website". Every face still NAMED Noto Sans Mono, HA Mono or HA
    Figures above now loads the typrighter files (Regular below 600, Bold
    from 600; figures Bold), so no rule — Luxe's, a section's or a template
    setting's — can draw Noto, and the stacks fall back to Junicode. The
    ha-noto-mono-*.woff2 assets are no longer requested.

    Later on 4 October (Ivan, "remove all noto-sans-mono in the whole
    website"): the faces NAMED Noto Sans Mono are gone too, the BAG takes the
    Typewriter Bold by --ha-font-record at 600, and the six ha-noto-mono-*
    files are deleted from the theme. Nothing on the site can name Noto.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Troja";
    src: url({{ 'ha-troja.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    2 October, later: Aloha sent the thinner cut, typrighter V1 Regular
    ("I have placed a thinner version for typrighter font … when we have
    info"). That is her rule 3, TYPEWRITER, for information; the Bold stays
    for rule 4, standalone numbers. One family, two faces by weight:
    100–599 Regular (every text role asks 400), 600–900 Bold (__num asks 700).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Text";
    src: url({{ 'ha-typewriter-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 599;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Text";
    src: url({{ 'ha-typewriter.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 600 900;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Text";
    src: url({{ 'ha-junicode-semibold-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-style: italic;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Note";
    src: url({{ 'ha-junicode-semibold-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-style: italic;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "HA Note";
    src: url({{ 'ha-junicode-semibold-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  :root {
    /* 2 October 2026 — see THE TYPOGRAPHY OF 2 OCTOBER above. The three old
       voice names keep working: narrate and record are Typewriter now, and
       identify is Porter with Typewriter figures and Typewriter behind it. */
    --ha-font-title:    "HA Troja", "Junicode", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --ha-font-text:     "HA Text", "Junicode", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    --ha-font-note:     "HA Note", "Junicode", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --ha-font-identify: {% if settings.ha_porter_licensed %}"Porter", "HA Porter At", "HA Figures Porter", {% endif %}"HA Text", "Junicode", ui-monospace, monospace;
    --ha-font-narrate:  var(--ha-font-text);
    --ha-font-record:   var(--ha-font-text);
    --ha-font-mono:     "HA Mono", "Junicode", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;

    /* ==================================================================
       THE FIVE ROLES  —  Aloha, 24 September 2026 (final typography system)

       One family and one weight per role. Sections name a ROLE, never a
       family or a weight; the classes that carry them are at the foot of
       assets/ha-sections.css ("TYPE ROLES"), where they have the last word.

       Porter is only the permanent navigation and the section labels now.
       Titles move to Junicode Light ("the distinction here is scale and
       context, rather than changing typeface"), and the old identify voice
       on buttons and links moves to the mono (now Typewriter) Medium.

       This reverses the 22 September table's voice rows (body copy and
       navigation in the condensed mono (retired)) — the switches in Theme
       settings > Typography voices now default to this system. The the mono
       Condensed options are kept only as a way back.
       ================================================================== */
    /* 2 October 2026: the role names stay, their faces follow her new rules. */
    --ha-role-title:         var(--ha-font-title);      /* 1 Troja */
    --ha-role-nav:           var(--ha-font-identify);   /* 2 Porter Medium (menu bar unchanged) */
    --ha-role-nav-weight:    500;
    --ha-role-nav-hover:     300;                         /*   hover: Porter Light */
    --ha-role-label:         var(--ha-font-identify);   /* 2 Porter Medium, as her labels are drawn */
    --ha-role-label-weight:  500;
    --ha-role-action:        var(--ha-font-identify);   /* 2 Porter Medium: buttons and text links */
    --ha-role-action-weight: 500;
    --ha-role-record:        var(--ha-font-text);       /* 3 Typewriter: data, prices, references */
    --ha-role-record-weight: 400;
    --ha-role-text:          var(--ha-font-text);       /* 3 Typewriter: body and information */
    --ha-role-text-weight:   400;
    --ha-role-number:        var(--ha-font-text);       /* 4 Typewriter Bold: standalone numbers */
    --ha-role-number-weight: 700;
    --ha-role-pull:          var(--ha-font-note);       /* 5 Junicode SemiBold Italic */
    --ha-role-pull-weight:   600;
    /* her paragraphs are the Typewriter at 82% opacity */
    --ha-text-alpha:         82%;

    {%- liquid
      assign body_voice = settings.ha_body_voice | default: 'narrate'
      assign chrome_voice = settings.ha_chrome_voice | default: 'identify'
    -%}
    {%- if body_voice == 'record' -%}
    --ha-voice-body: var(--ha-font-mono);
    --ha-voice-body-weight: 400;
    {%- else -%}
    --ha-voice-body: var(--ha-role-text);
    --ha-voice-body-weight: var(--ha-role-text-weight);
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if chrome_voice == 'record' -%}
    --ha-voice-chrome: var(--ha-font-mono);
    --ha-voice-chrome-weight: 400;
    --ha-voice-chrome-hover: 400;
    {%- else -%}
    --ha-voice-chrome: var(--ha-role-nav);
    --ha-voice-chrome-weight: var(--ha-role-nav-weight);
    --ha-voice-chrome-hover: var(--ha-role-nav-hover);
    {%- endif -%}

    /* override Luxe's font_picker-generated families.

       --font-body-family is the family every unmarked word on the site
       inherits — Luxe's cart, account pages, forms, facets, cards and the
       cookie banner included. Pointing it at the body voice is what makes
       "the condensed mono (retired) = body copy […] functional information" true
       across the whole theme rather than only in the Hartwick sections. */
    /* Titles are Junicode Light (roles 04/05), so Luxe's headings are too. */
    --font-heading-family: var(--ha-role-title);
    --font-heading-weight: 400;
    --font-heading-style: normal;
    --font-body-family:    var(--ha-voice-body);
    /* Luxe gives buttons the accent family with !important: Porter, role 2 */
    --font-accent-family:  var(--ha-role-action);

    /* Luxe derives these from the old Swiss 721 font picker (weight 400).
       The brand book set Junicode body copy and editorial display at Medium;
       Aloha overruled that on 18 September 2026: "All Junicode fonts are always
       Light, and when it's in Italics, it's also Light Italic." Junicode is
       therefore 300 wherever it appears, and so is its bold — <strong> in
       Junicode no longer changes weight (the italic face is the emphasis
       available). The variable file still carries 300-700 because the landing
       page's headline is set in Junicode Bold by its own design and is not
       part of this rule.

       The body weight now follows the body voice: 300 while Junicode carries
       body copy, 400 once the mono does. */
    --font-body-weight: var(--ha-voice-body-weight);
    --font-body-weight-bold: var(--ha-voice-body-weight);
    --font-body-style: normal;
    /* Price is a record row in Aloha's table (12px, the mono), so it takes the
       record weight. It followed Junicode's 300 while prices were set in
       Junicode. */
    --price-font-weight: var(--ha-role-record-weight);
  }

  /* No synthetic bold in any voice. The browser default for <strong> and <b>
     is "bolder", which lifts Junicode Light (300) to 400 — that is what put the
     shipping note's opening sentence a weight above its paragraph — and which
     makes the browser fake a bold for the mono, whose 700 is not loaded. Emphasis
     keeps its parent's weight everywhere; italic remains the emphasis available
     in Junicode. Shopify's cookie-consent banner sets its own heading bold,
     hence the id-qualified override. */
  strong, b { font-weight: inherit; }
  #shopify-pc__banner h2 { font-weight: inherit; }

  /* IDENTIFY — brand book: uppercase only, tracking +20 to +80, line height 90-110%

     `!important` on the family is deliberate and is the only one of the three
     voices that needs it. Luxe's base.css carries

         button, .button, .link--underlined, .product-form__input,
         div[role="button"], .shopify-challenge__button, .account-sub-navigation
         { font-family: var(--font-accent-family) !important; }

     which put every primary control — Add to Bag, Join The Register, the
     appointment submit — into the RECORD voice no matter what class we gave it.
     A voice class that any theme rule can silently overrule is not a voice
     class. `.ha-identify` is our own opt-in marker, applied only where Porter is
     wanted, so making it authoritative is safe and fixes every current and
     future case at once rather than one button at a time. */
  /* 24 September 2026: .ha-identify is now role 02, the section label —
     Porter LIGHT. Buttons, links and titles that used to carry it have moved
     to .ha-record (the mono (now Typewriter) Medium) and .ha-narrate (Junicode Light);
     what still carries it is a label. .ha-label is the role's own name. */
  .ha-identify,
  .ha-label {
    font-family: var(--ha-role-label) !important;
    font-weight: var(--ha-role-label-weight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* NARRATE — brand book: body line height 140-155%, tracking 0 to +10.
     Always Light (see the weight note above): stated here so that a heading
     given this voice takes 300 rather than Luxe's font-picker heading weight. */
  .ha-narrate {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-narrate);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
  }

  /* RECORD — brand book: uppercase labels, tabular numerals, left aligned.

     `font-weight: 400` is explicit because the condensed mono (retired) ships in
     ONE weight here and Luxe's `--font-body-weight` asks for 500. Asking a
     400-only face for 500 makes the browser synthesise bold, which it does
     unevenly from run to run — that is why the footer policy links looked like
     a mix of bold and regular. Requesting the weight the file actually has
     removes the synthesis entirely. */
  .ha-record {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-record);
    font-weight: var(--ha-role-record-weight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* NAVIGATION — role 01, Porter Medium (Aloha, 24 September 2026: "reserved
     for the permanent website navigation and global utility areas […]
     Default state: Porter Medium. Hover / selected state: Porter Light.").
     It follows --ha-voice-chrome so the 22 September the mono option remains one
     setting away. Luxe's base.css assigns --font-accent-family to
     .header-bar-inner with !important; these selectors are more specific, so
     they win either way. Porter Light is 1.5% narrower than Medium (about a
     pixel on COLLECTION at 12px), so the hover swap does not jog the bar. */
  .hdr-nav-primary-level-ul a,
  .nav-ul--primary a,
  .nav-ul--secondary a,
  /* the utility side of the bar is navigation as well — Bag, Account, Search */
  .header-bar .cart-icon--bubble,
  .header-bar a[href*="/cart"],
  .header-bar a[href*="/account"],
  /* the shopping-tools labels — Search, Account, Bag. Search renders as
     `.hdr-st-item-label` inside a <button>, so it was still being caught by
     Luxe's `button { … !important }` rule and sitting in the RECORD voice while
     the links either side of it were in Porter. */
  .header-bar--shopping-tools .hdr-st-item,
  .header-bar--shopping-tools .hdr-st-item-label,
  .hdr-search-btn .hdr-st-item-label,
  .cart-count-bubble {
    font-family: var(--ha-voice-chrome) !important;
    /* UPPERCASE IS NOT DECORATION HERE — it is required while Porter carries
       this surface.

       Porter is subset to A-Z and space (the brand rule: no numbers,
       punctuation or symbols). A label typed in sentence case therefore renders
       its capital in Porter and every lowercase letter in Junicode, because the
       glyphs simply are not in the file. "Account" — which comes from a
       translation string, not from the menu — was rendering as "A" in Porter
       and "ccount" in Junicode, which is what made it look like a different
       font and size from the menu items above it.

       Uppercasing every Porter surface guarantees a single face. Any label an
       editor types in mixed case is covered automatically. */
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* Porter Medium at rest (role 01). Luxe sets the bar's weight with
       !important, hence the same here. */
    font-weight: var(--ha-voice-chrome-weight) !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    /* Aloha's table: navigation is 11px, line height 1.2. Luxe's header section
       sets its own sizes from section settings, which are set to match; this is
       the backstop for any nav surface the section does not name. */
    font-size: var(--ha-t-nav);
    line-height: var(--ha-t-lh-nav);
  }
  /* …and Porter Light on hover, keyboard focus and the current page. */
  .hdr-nav-primary-level-ul a:hover,
  .hdr-nav-primary-level-ul a:focus-visible,
  .hdr-nav-primary-level-ul a[aria-current="page"],
  .nav-ul--primary a:hover,
  .nav-ul--primary a:focus-visible,
  .nav-ul--primary a[aria-current="page"],
  .nav-ul--secondary a:hover,
  .nav-ul--secondary a:focus-visible,
  .header-bar a[href*="/cart"]:hover,
  .header-bar a[href*="/account"]:hover,
  .header-bar--shopping-tools .hdr-st-item:hover,
  .header-bar--shopping-tools .hdr-st-item:hover .hdr-st-item-label {
    font-weight: var(--ha-voice-chrome-hover) !important;
  }

  /* BAG — the one deliberate exception in the bar (Aloha, 24 September 2026):
     "The only font that is different from the rest is: THE MONO (NOW TYPEWRITER) →
     Semibold", the normal-width mono (the Condensed cut is retired). Same size
     and tracking as the navigation; it does not change weight on hover. The
     id makes it outrank the navigation rule above, which also matches it. */
  #SiteHeader .hdr-st-item-cart,
  #SiteHeader .hdr-st-item-cart .cart-icon--bubble,
  #SiteHeader .hdr-st-item-cart .cart-icon--bubble *,
  #SiteHeader .hdr-st-item-cart .cart-icon--bubble:hover,
  #SiteHeader .hdr-st-item-cart .cart-icon--bubble:hover * {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-record) !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important;
    font-size: var(--ha-t-nav);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Wordmark. Colour comes from `color` because the SVG paints with currentColor:
     Inkstone on light grounds, Chalk Blue on dark. Logo rules give a 220px digital
     minimum width — below that the framed House Symbol must be used instead. */
  .ha-wordmark {
    display: block;
    width: 220px;
    max-width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1225.9 / 301.7;
    color: var(--ha-inkstone);
  }
  .ha-wordmark--invert { color: var(--ha-chalk-blue); }
{% endstyle %}
